  "title": "Ratio-analysis briefing",
  "html": "<div class=\"course-intro-card\"><h2>Ratio-analysis briefing</h2><p>Prepare ratios and evaluate a liquidity concern using the stated definitions.</p></div><section class=\"quiz-card\"><h3>Required responses</h3><div class=\"tbs-question\"><label for=\"bar-m1-tbs1-f1\">Current ratio</label><input id=\"bar-m1-tbs1-f1\" type=\"text\"></div><div class=\"tbs-question\"><label for=\"bar-m1-tbs1-f2\">Quick ratio</label><input id=\"bar-m1-tbs1-f2\" type=\"text\"></div><div class=\"tbs-question\"><label for=\"bar-m1-tbs1-f3\">Gross margin percentage</label><input id=\"bar-m1-tbs1-f3\" type=\"text\"></div><div class=\"tbs-question\"><label for=\"bar-m1-tbs1-f4\">Interpretation of aging inventory</label><select id=\"bar-m1-tbs1-f4\"><option value=\"Evaluate realizability before concluding liquidity improved\">Evaluate realizability before concluding liquidity improved</option><option value=\"Assume the ratio proves strong liquidity\">Assume the ratio proves strong liquidity</option><option value=\"Ignore operating information\">Ignore operating information</option><option value=\"Treat all inventory as cash\">Treat all inventory as cash</option></select></div></section>",
